       "md": "- **Econometrics**: $\\mathrm{tr}(\\mathbf{M}) = n - K$ gives $E[\\mathbf{e}'\\mathbf{e}] = (n-K)\\sigma^2$ and the unbiased $\\widehat{\\sigma}^2$ ([Projection Matrix and Residual Maker](note:projection-matrix-and-residual-maker), [Sampling Distribution of OLS](note:sampling-distribution-of-ols)); leverages sum to $K$ ([Regression Diagnostics](note:regression-diagnostics))."
      }
